    <section id="rs-profile">
        <h3>Profile</h3>
        <p>Builder-oriented product, technology, and innovation executive with 19 years across software development, digital experience, creative technology, agency leadership, and enterprise AI. Turns emerging capability into products people adopt: the right context for agents, connections to the systems where work already happens, and a path from prototype to production. Most recently VP, Creative Innovation at Mod Op, where I led product and technical direction for Nexus, the platform at the core of Orion, the agency's AI operating layer, and owned six products in the portfolio. Nexus turned a proposed shared foundation into a working one: identity and permissions, shared knowledge, agents, a chat workspace, and measurement to prove it was being used. Mod Op reported 95% employee adoption and 700+ agents at Orion's public launch in July 2026.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="rs-expertise">
        <h3>Expertise</h3>
        <p><strong>AI products &amp; platforms.</strong> Enterprise AI &middot; LLM applications &middot; Agents &middot; RAG and retrieval &middot; Context engineering &middot; Knowledge architecture &middot; MCP and A2A &middot; Human-in-the-loop agent workflows &middot; AI evaluation &middot; Generative image systems</p>
        <p><strong>Product &amp; innovation.</strong> Product vision and strategy &middot; Portfolio prioritization &middot; Rapid prototyping &middot; Prototype-to-MVP systems &middot; Roadmaps &middot; Adoption measurement &middot; Build/buy/extend decisions</p>
        <p><strong>Leadership &amp; commercialization.</strong> Cross-functional leadership &middot; Enterprise transformation &middot; Executive communication &middot; Client advisory &middot; Prototype-led selling &middot; Organizational enablement</p>
        <p><strong>Technical foundation.</strong> Next.js &middot; PostgreSQL &middot; OAuth 2.0 / SSO &middot; OpenAI APIs &middot; Modern web architecture &middot; AI-assisted development with Claude Code and Cursor &middot; UX and product architecture</p>
