    <section id="rs-history">
        <h3>Chronology</h3>
        <p>
            <strong>Mod Op</strong> &middot; Vice President, Creative Innovation <span class="when">Nov 2024&ndash;Aug 2026</span><br />
            Founding member of the Innovation team and member of Mod Op's AI Council, which defined responsible-use practice and compliance protocols. Led a six-person product and engineering team in the company's first product engineering group, responsible for identifying AI technologies worth adopting, rolling them out internally, and finding ways to deploy them for clients.
            <br /><br />
            Led product and technical direction for <strong><a href="/nexus">Nexus</a></strong>, the platform at the core of Orion, Mod Op's AI operating layer (known publicly as Mod Engine, Mod Chat, and Orion). Nexus turned a proposed shared foundation into a working one: identity and permissions tied to the organization and the user, Knowledge Layers of approved company and brand context, a growing library of agents, a model-agnostic chat harness, and MCP access from tools such as Claude Code and Cursor. Mod Op reported 95% employee adoption and 700+ agents at Orion's July 2026 launch, and Digiday cited roughly $3M in avoided licensing costs across the platform.
            <br /><br />
            Owned six products in the portfolio, Nexus included. <strong>Brand Agents</strong>: persistent brand-aware assistants launched April 2025, with 50+ client-specific agents by June 2025; wrote the launch article. <strong><a href="/mod-heat">Mod Heat</a></strong>: originated the concept in February 2024, pitched it to the executive team, and shipped it in Q4 2024, building in an unfamiliar stack with Cursor; Mod Op launched it publicly in October 2025. <strong><a href="/geo">GEO by Mod Op</a></strong>: took the concept from Launchpad to a live product and designed its commercial model, the portfolio's first directly paid offering; live June 18, 2026 at <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">geo.modop.ai</a>, launched publicly by Mod Op in August 2026, and the system behind its GEO 50 benchmark. <strong><a href="/launchpad">Launchpad</a></strong>: self-serve framework for deploying prototype tools and agents with governance, evaluation, and a path to production; dozens of prototypes from Q1 2026 hackathons. <strong>Audience Lab</strong>: digital-twin audience simulation for creative pretesting. Prototype-led work drove active pipeline conversations with dozens of client accounts by August 2026.
            <br /><br />
            Appeared on five episodes of Mod Op's Leader Generation podcast (Cursor, Brand Agents, vibe coding, MCP and A2A, context engineering) and wrote Mod Op's public articles on Brand Agents and micro-tools.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Red Tettemer O'Connell + Partners</strong> &middot; Technology Director <span class="when">May 2010&ndash;Nov 2024</span><br />
            Staff engineer, then tech lead, then technology director over fourteen years. Led multidisciplinary teams across engineering, UX, creative, strategy, production, and analytics for clients including NBCUniversal, Under Armour, Planet Fitness, FOX, Sheetz, Swarovski, Stanley Black+Decker, Kellogg's, William Grant &amp; Sons, Dietz &amp; Watson, and Sparkling Ice. Co-led the agency's first all-hands on generative AI in Q4 2022; created the Frontier AI briefing; built early branded Stable Diffusion demonstrations in 2023; worked with client teams through the first wave of AI transformation. Mod Op acquired the agency in 2024; tenure continuous.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Cubist Media Group</strong> &middot; Interactive Developer <span class="when">Sep 2007&ndash;May 2010</span><br />
            Built websites, web applications, and DVD/Blu-ray titles for Warner Bros., NFL Films, and Bethesda Softworks.
        </p>
